{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1564664-a-gotham-for-trinity","id":1564664,"title":"A \"Gotham\" for Trinity","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-10-10T08:11:01-07:00","id":1564664,"title":"A \"Gotham\" for Trinity","content":"It\u2019s been way too long since I\u2019ve had a chance to dive back into Trinity. Now it\u2019s time to do so again. We recently started wondering where, when, and how something like Gotham City could fit into the Trinity Continuum. In other words, a gloomy, modern yet somehow antiquated-looking metropolis with ornate skyscrapers, an atmosphere that could vaguely be described as \u201cGothic,\u201d plenty of crime, and a whole bunch of lunatics\u2014both costumed and not. <br /> In the era of \u201cAdventure!,\u201d this is admittedly almost trivial. Just take New York, Chicago, or any other major U.S. city and throw in a few masked figures. That might still work pretty well for \u201cContinuum,\u201d too.<br /> <br /> When it came to \u201cAeon,\u201d we wondered if Berlin might not actually work quite well as a \u201cgloomy Gotham stand-in.\u201d Despite everything, the city is still a metropolis with a population of over a million in 2130; however, due to the poor overall state of Europe, it is likely to have a very high crime rate.Furthermore, if one goes by the descriptions in the first edition, \u201cNew Weimar\u201d is a \u201cnostalgic\u201d nation, oriented more toward past greatness than toward the future\u2014a fact that may also be reflected in its architecture. What if, by around 2080, Berlin\u2019s architecture had already been oriented more toward the past\u2014what if new skyscrapers and arcologies had been built\u2014and what if the city now actually looked like Fritz Lang\u2019s *Metropolis* with gargoyles? (And much of it is already falling apart again by now.) What if we add a few local fads inspired by Berlin\u2019s so-called \u201cgolden years\u201d of the 1920s? Throw in a few Psiads, \u201cRing clubs\u201d (organized crime), strange Aberrant cults, and rampant corruption\u2014and there you have it.<br /> <br /> But how and where on earth could you fit a \u201cGotham\u201d into \u201cAberrant\u201d?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24955-waldi","name":"Waldi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}